/-!
# The exact Nieuwland number of `Antiprism.HexagonalAntiprism.polyhedron`

`prismHexagonalAntiprism_exact`: the Nieuwland number of `Antiprism.HexagonalAntiprism.polyhedron` is the largest value of the scale `ℓ` over the
real solutions of the contact system below (the root's: the scale `ℓ`, the pose `s t r1 r2 r3` and translation `u1 u2`, the multipliers `m0 m1 …`, the field's generator `g` and the coordinates `p3x p3y p3z …` of the vertices in contact; each unknown of the root's system in its box), and it lies between the two decimals. The statement is written with free
variables and integer polynomials (`Modules/System/Readable.lean`); it is proved from
`prismHexagonalAntiprism_exact_list`, the same statement in the list form of `Modules/System/System.lean`
(`Readable.isGreatest`: the written polynomials are the list form's, checked by the kernel, and
the statement's text is the list form's written form by definition). The root's system has exactly one zero in its box (Krawczyk's test, `prismHexagonalAntiprism_nieuwland`), so its written-out system has exactly one solution, whose scale is the number (`Root.isMaxSingle_one`).
Generated by `lean/scripts/exact_n.py` from the certificate's theorems in `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandPrismHexagonalAntiprism`.
-/

namespace Nieuwland.Polyhedra

open Check

